  "nl_text": "The database schema named \"schemabench_0163\" consists of 8 tables. The primary purpose of this schema is to manage various aspects of event planning and administration.\nThe CUSTOMER table represents customers who are interested in hosting events. It contains columns for customer number, name, address, internal status, contact information, phone number, city, state, and zip code. The CUSTNO column is the primary key.\nThe FACILITY table represents facilities that can host events. It contains columns for facility number and name. The FACNO column is the primary key and the FACNAME column is unique.\nThe LOCATION table represents locations within these facilities. It contains columns for location number, facility number, and location name. The LOCNO column is the primary key and the FACNO column is a foreign key referencing the FACILITY table.\nThe EVENTREQUEST table represents requests for events. It contains columns for event number, date held, date required, facility number, customer number, date authorized, status, estimated cost, estimated audience, and budget number. The EVENTNO column is the primary key, and the CUSTNO and FACNO columns are foreign keys referencing the CUSTOMER and FACILITY tables respectively. The STATUS column has a check constraint to ensure its value is either 'Pending', 'Denied', or 'Approved'. The ESTAUDIENCE column has a check constraint to ensure its value is greater than 0.\nThe EMPLOYEE table represents employees who work at the facility. It contains columns for employee number, name, department, email, and phone number. The EMPNO column is the primary key.\nThe EVENTPLAN table represents plans for events. It contains columns for plan number, event number, work date, notes, activity, and employee number. The PLANNO column is the primary key and the EVENTNO and EMPNO columns are foreign keys referencing the EVENTREQUEST and EMPLOYEE tables respectively.\nThe RESOURCETBL table represents resources used in event planning. It contains columns for resource number, name, and rate. The RESNO column is the primary key. The RATE column has a check constraint to ensure its value is greater than 0.\nThe EVENTPLANLINE table represents lines in event plans. It contains columns for plan number, line number, time start, time end, number of people, location number, and resource number. The LINENO and PLANNO columns form a composite primary key. The PLANNO column is a foreign key referencing the EVENTPLAN table, and the LOCNO and RESNO columns are foreign keys referencing the LOCATION and RESOURCETBL tables respectively. The TIMESTART and TIMEEND columns have a check constraint to ensure the start time is before the end time.",
  "gold_question": "1) Background / Context:\nThe project involves the development of a system to manage athletic events efficiently. This system is centered around the collaboration between customers, employees, and the facilities where events take place. It focuses on ensuring streamlined event planning and resource allocation.\n\n2) Objectives:\n- Facilitate the request and management of athletic events.\n- Enable efficient coordination of event plans and associated resources.\n- Ensure accurate record-keeping for customers, facilities, and event details.\n\n3) Stakeholders & Users:\n- Customers: Individuals or organizations that request events.\n- Employees: Staff responsible for managing event plans.\n- Facility Managers: Personnel overseeing venue availability and assignment.\n\n4) Functional Descriptions:\n- Customer Management: Store and maintain customer details, allowing them to request events.\n- Event Request Processing: Allow customers to submit event requests, specifying desired dates, costs, and audience size. Requests must be approved, pending, or denied.\n- Employee Management: Keep track of employees who manage event plans.\n- Event Planning: Develop detailed event plans including timeline and assigned resources. Each plan is managed by an employee and linked to an event request.\n- Resource Allocation: Assign resources such as equipment to event plans, ensuring availability and proper cost management.\n- Location and Facility Management: Manage facility locations and link them to event plans, ensuring proper tracking and availability.\n\n5) Non-Functional Descriptions:\n- Data Integrity: Maintain accuracy and consistency across tables, with constraints to ensure valid statuses, audience estimates, and resource rates.\n- Security: Ensure that data access is controlled and restricted to authorized users.\n- Scalability: Support a growing number of event requests and plans without degradation in performance.\n- Usability: Provide an intuitive interface for customers to request events and employees to manage plans efficiently.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_deepseek/0163.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0163\nCREATE TABLE `customer` (\n  `custno` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `internal_status` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `contact_info` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `city` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `state` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `zip_code` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`custno`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `facility` (\n  `facno` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `facname` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`facno`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `facname_UNIQUE` (`facname`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `location` (\n  `locno` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `facno` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `location_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`locno`),\n  CONSTRAINT `location_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`facno`) REFERENCES `facility` (`facno`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `eventrequest` (\n  `eventno` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `date_held` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `date_required` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `facno` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `custno` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `date_authorized` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `status` enum('Pending', 'Denied', 'Approved') NOT NULL,\n  `estimated_cost` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `estaudience` int(11) CHECK (`estaudience` > 0),\n  `budget_number` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`eventno`),\n  CONSTRAINT `eventrequest_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`custno`) REFERENCES `customer` (`custno`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `eventrequest_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`facno`) REFERENCES `facility` (`facno`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `employee` (\n  `empno` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `department` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`empno`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `eventplan` (\n  `planno` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `eventno` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `work_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `notes` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `activity` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `empno` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`planno`),\n  CONSTRAINT `eventplan_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`eventno`) REFERENCES `eventrequest` (`eventno`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `eventplan_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`empno`) REFERENCES `employee` (`empno`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `resourcetbl` (\n  `resno` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `rate` decimal(10,2) CHECK (`rate` > 0) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`resno`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `eventplanline` (\n  `planno` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `lineno` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `time_start` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `time_end` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `number_of_people` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `locno` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `resno` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`planno`, `lineno`),\n  CONSTRAINT `eventplanline_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`planno`) REFERENCES `eventplan` (`planno`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `eventplanline_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`locno`) REFERENCES `location` (`locno`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `eventplanline_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`resno`) REFERENCES `resourcetbl` (`resno`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CHECK (`time_start` < `time_end`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
